  "assumptions": [
    "USB-C input is a 5 V sink using standard CC pull-downs; no higher-voltage PD contract is required (defaulted)",
    "+5V is the protected, distributed VBUS rail and is distinct from raw VBUS by input protection/filtering (defaulted)",
    "3.3 V regulation uses TLV62569DBVR, rated for approximately 1 A output from 5 V (defaulted)",
    "ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R8 uses native USB for programming with onboard USB-C data connectivity and no USB-UART bridge (defaulted)",
    "HUB75 interface uses the hub75-sn74hct245-interface recipe and common HUB75 signal naming (defaulted)",
    "Addressable LED output uses WS2812B-B/T signaling with a 5 V external-string supply and series data resistor (defaulted)",
    "Speaker output is a low-power external PWM speaker connector; no audio amplifier IC is added because the brief requests an output (defaulted)",
    "Larger ESP32-S3-WROOM-1 module is retained because the named N16R8 part is explicit (defaulted)",
    "USB programming power is host-supplied VBUS and is not tied to a battery or alternate board power source (defaulted)"
  ],
